I have enough to conclude. The findings are below; the JSON is the final output.

```json
{
  "root_causes": [
    {
      "service": "ts-preserve-service",
      "fault_kind": "http_response_body_corrupted",
      "evidence": [
        {"kind": "trace", "sql": "SELECT service_name, span_name, attr_span_kind, attr_http_response_status_code, attr_status_code, count(*) n FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name='ts-preserve-service' AND attr_span_kind='Client' GROUP BY ALL", "claim": "All 1603 outgoing GET calls from ts-preserve-service to security return HTTP 404 with Error status during the incident."},
        {"kind": "trace", "sql": "SELECT 'ab' p, service_name, span_name, attr_span_kind, attr_http_response_status_code code, attr_status_code, count(*) n FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name='ts-security-service' AND attr_span_kind='Server' GROUP BY ALL UNION ALL SELECT 'norm', service_name, span_name, attr_span_kind, attr_http_response_status_code, attr_status_code, count(*) FROM normal_traces WHERE service_name='ts-security-service' AND attr_span_kind='Server' GROUP BY ALL", "claim": "Security normally serves GET securityConfigs/{accountId} with 200; during the incident only unmatched GET /** 404s occur, so the request path was altered upstream."},
        {"kind": "log", "sql": "SELECT service_name, level, attr_log_template, count(*) n FROM abnormal_logs WHERE service_name='ts-preserve-service' AND level IN ('SEVERE','ERROR') GROUP BY ALL", "claim": "ts-preserve-service logs a SEVERE 'Request processing failed' exception on all 1603 preserve requests."}
      ]
    },
    {
      "service": "ts-user-service",
      "fault_kind": "application_method_slow",
      "evidence": [
        {"kind": "trace", "sql": "SELECT service_name, span_name, attr_span_kind, count(*) n, round(avg(CASE WHEN p='ab' THEN duration END)/1e6,2) ab_ms, round(avg(CASE WHEN p='norm' THEN duration END)/1e6,2) norm_ms FROM (SELECT 'ab' p,* FROM abnormal_traces UNION ALL SELECT 'norm',* FROM normal_traces) WHERE service_name='ts-user-service' AND span_name IN ('UserController.getUserByUserId','UserRepository.findByUserId','SELECT User') GROUP BY ALL", "claim": "getUserByUserId self-time rises from about 3 ms to 18 ms while its DB query stays about 1.4 ms."},
        {"kind": "trace", "sql": "SELECT 'ab' p, span_name, count(*) n, round(avg(duration)/1e6,2) avg_ms FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name='ts-ui-dashboard' AND span_name='GET /api/v1/userservice/users/id/{userId}' GROUP BY ALL UNION ALL SELECT 'norm', span_name, count(*), round(avg(duration)/1e6,2) FROM normal_traces WHERE service_name='ts-ui-dashboard' AND span_name='GET /api/v1/userservice/users/id/{userId}' GROUP BY ALL", "claim": "Dashboard's user lookup latency rises from about 8 ms to 23 ms, matching the slower user-service server span."}
      ]
    }
  ],
  "propagation": [
    {"from": "ts-preserve-service", "to": "ts-ui-dashboard", "evidence": [{"kind": "trace", "sql": "SELECT attr_status_code, attr_http_response_status_code, count(*) n, round(avg(duration)/1e6,1) avg_ms FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name='ts-ui-dashboard' AND span_name='POST /api/v1/preserveservice/preserve' GROUP BY ALL", "claim": "89 of 111 user preserve requests at ts-ui-dashboard return 500 after about 3.5 s, as preserve fails."}]},
    {"from": "ts-user-service", "to": "ts-ui-dashboard", "evidence": [{"kind": "trace", "sql": "SELECT 'ab' p, span_name, count(*) n, round(avg(duration)/1e6,2) avg_ms FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name='ts-user-service' AND attr_span_kind='Server' GROUP BY ALL UNION ALL SELECT 'norm', span_name, count(*), round(avg(duration)/1e6,2) FROM normal_traces WHERE service_name='ts-user-service' AND attr_span_kind='Server' GROUP BY ALL", "claim": "User-service server span for users/id rises from about 5 ms to 20 ms, which the dashboard inherits as slower user lookups."}]}
  ]
}
```

**Summary of findings**

- **Affected user-facing path:** `POST /api/v1/preserveservice/preserve` at `ts-ui-dashboard`. It returned 500 on 89 of 111 requests, at about 3.5 s average versus 0.36 s normally. Users see failed bookings.
- **Fault 1, `ts-preserve-service` (`http_response_body_corrupted`):** Preserve's `checkSecurity` call to `ts-security-service` changed from the normal `GET /api/v1/securityservice/securityConfigs/{accountId}` (200) to a path that matches no route (404 on `GET /**`). Security's own server behaviour is consistent with the path being altered in transit, so the fault is in the caller's outgoing request. Every preserve request then fails with a SEVERE log. Hubble and container metrics show no connection-level drop or loss, which rules out a network fault.
- **Fault 2, `ts-user-service` (`application_method_slow`):** `UserController.getUserByUserId` self-time grew from about 3 ms to 18 ms, while its DB span stayed about 1.4 ms. Its JVM and container CPU and memory showed no resource pressure, and the dashboard-to-user gap stayed small, so this is in-process slowness, not network. It is a separate fault, and it slows the user lookup at `ts-ui-dashboard`.
- **Ruled out:** No Kubernetes restarts or pod changes appeared. Network counters rose in line with the load increase, with no per-connection anomaly. Other services' changes were small or consistent with load.
